comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T18:27:55.681Z",codex-agent,"Related prior SDK adoption: pm-slack-standup-xms9; certified-reader work: pm-slack-standup-ozic. Plan: host client.listAllComplete with existing certification; settings-derived lifecycle registry; SDK expected errors. Keep the public synchronous fetchAllItems(pmRoot, pmBin) standalone executable adapter for compatibility. Verify history after SDK cache priming, compare immutable public tracker copies, and record one behavioural revert per replacement."
  "2026-10-25T18:36:53.037Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: hosted standup, alias, decisions and exporter reads now use the invocation SDK client.listAllComplete({ includeBody: true }), retain readCompleteStandupItems/certifyCompleteListResult, and call the fresh SDK history verification action before rows can drive output or snapshots. The synchronous fetchAllItems(pmRoot, pmBin) API remains only as the explicit standalone executable adapter: PmClient.listAllComplete is asynchronous and cannot preserve its synchronous/executable-selection contract. No missing upstream SDK API blocks hosted adoption. SDK EXIT_CODE/createPmCliExpectedError replace local error ownership; CommandError remains a compatibility wrapper for instanceof consumers. Lifecycle buckets use readSettings/resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry/statusIsTerminal with legacy presentation aliases. Host peer and manifest floors now require 2026.10.20; development dependency pin unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T18:36:57.237Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs: replacing only readSdkStandupItems with the previous fetchAllItems call makes the no-git/no-executable regression fail (exit 127). Restoring the original buildStandupData function and its removed status constants makes the custom-terminal regression fail: expected custom-done but got no done item. Restoring only the previous CommandError class makes the SDK expected-error discriminator assertion fail. All three experiments ran the same test/sdk-adoption.test.ts regressions via node --test --test-name-pattern and each exited nonzero; the adopted implementation passes 4/4 focused tests. Corruption-after-cache test verifies both command refusal and absence of export/snapshot files."
  "2026-10-25T18:38:14.729Z",codex-agent,"Public differential proof: immutable origin/main build 523c0786f085db52d585a7714598c90d38eeb3d0 versus adoption, with identical pinned dependencies. PUBLIC repository archives: pm-slack-standup at that build (100 items) and pm-slack at 5c0bd37fa16a42956c6b2e33e491163f04a3d9a9 (89 items). In non-git scratch tracker copies, all 22 command/export comparisons match exactly (standup and slack-standup in plain/markdown/slack/blockkit, decisions, md/json export). Printed stdout and handler results match; authoritative tracker byte hashes remain unchanged. No real-corpus intentional differences observed. Synthetic tests cover documented stricter custom-terminal/canceled-blocker/history behavior. Reproducer: test/sdk-adoption-differential.test.ts with STANDUP_DIFFERENTIAL_TRACKERS as a JSON array of additional public tracker copies."
  "2026-10-25T18:41:23.955Z",codex-agent,"Linked pinned-pm test execution completed successfully: node --test test/sdk-adoption.test.ts passes 4/4. The item has a related_to dependency on pm-slack-standup-xms9 and remains in progress for final gates and review. npm typecheck/build:test and lint pass; the standalone duplication gate reports 0% (0/10048 lines). Full all-source coverage and release evidence are still pending."
  "2026-10-25T18:42:49.080Z",codex-agent,"Additional integrity revert proof: removing only the fresh history verification loop makes the corruption-after-cache test fail with Missing expected rejection (exit 1); restoring it passes. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication gate, build and docstring gates pass (12 source files, 104 documented declarations), with 4/4 focused tests. Initial full coverage run reached 100% statements/lines/functions and 99.91% branches, with one unexercised error-formatting branch; simplified that formatting without reducing thresholds. An existing packed-acceptance subprocess timed out in that run; full serial gates will be rerun. Health under inherited global extensions reported host version skew; isolated-home health is the CI-relevant check."
  "2026-10-25T18:58:43.195Z",codex-agent,"Final source verification: isolated-home npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass. Each reports 280/280 suite tests, 1/1 canonical-reader acceptance and 5/5 packed acceptance scenarios. All 12 executable source files retain 100% lines/statements/functions/branches: 4055/4055 lines and statements, 143/143 functions, 1245/1245 branches; zero exclusions and unchanged thresholds. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, production audit, packaging, changelog and attestation gates pass. Isolated-home strict tracker health passes. Final-source differential rerun passes 22/22 exact comparisons across public 100-item and 89-item corpora, with authoritative byte inventories unchanged. Four behavioural revert experiments are documented in docs/sdk-adoption-validation.md. The patch removes 56 index.ts source lines (129 deleted tracked lines including generated/config replacements). Ready for PR and CI review; no upstream SDK blockers identified."
  "2026-10-25T20:52:35.281Z",codex-agent,"Review continuation for PR 151: the configured reviewing active-role status is omitted because buildStandupData compares one in_progress_status name. Reusing this adoption item. Plan: audit all lifecycle decisions, centralize SDK registry role classification, include decision-request suppression and blocker rendering, preserve legacy aliases only in the default presentation registry, and exercise randomized registries/items across selection flags and filters. No merge or release; no review thread replies."
  "2026-10-25T21:02:38.702Z",codex-agent,"Role-class closure: status-roles.ts classifyStandupItem is now the only item lifecycle classifier. Removed single-name active/open checks and the decision collector terminal-name set; routed work bucketing, stale-blocker age, normal/compact blocker markers and direct/periodic decision suppression through SDK role sets, definitions, alias normalization and terminal resolution. Default standalone compatibility aliases are SDK registry configuration and never override tracker-defined roles. Property oracle: 64 SDK registries, 3840 bucket cases, 61440 section selections, 223200 item classifications; no missing or duplicated eligible items across all all-open/include-done choices, five team modes and three windows. Includes multiple statuses per role, renamed workflow defaults, overlapping roles and misleading conventional names. Real no-git tracker verifies reviewing active work, additional open-role work and custom terminal decisions through previews/exports. Four isolated revert proofs fail: singleton active, singleton open, terminal blocker bypass and hard-coded decision terminal suppression; restoring the helper passes 7/7 new plus integrity-focused tests. Remaining status comparisons are input shape, process/HTTP exits, grouping options or versioned declaration state, not tracker lifecycle meaning. Typecheck/lint/zero duplication/docstrings/build pass; full gates pending."
  "2026-10-25T21:12:49.197Z",codex-agent,"First role-closure full gate: 282/283 tests passed; status-roles.ts itself measured 100/100/100/100. The sole failing legacy assertion deliberately removed an item status and expected silent omission. Updated it to require the new explicit unregistered-status refusal mandated by the no-disappearing-items contract; no production behavior or gate threshold was weakened. The source-copy documentation test now copies the new status-roles.ts module. Corrected targeted typecheck/build:test/lint/zero-duplication checks pass; full release gates are being rerun."
  "2026-10-25T21:26:30.789Z",codex-agent,"Corrected full-suite run measured all 13 sources at 100/100/100/100. The sole failure is the pre-existing packed acceptance subprocess timeout (290 seconds), with no role/integrity regression failure. Retrying the unchanged release command with a two-CPU affinity bound, reducing available parallelism from four CPUs; no test scope, timeout, threshold or workflow changes. The corrected targeted run passes 11/11."
  "2026-10-25T22:04:34.605Z",codex-agent,"Final status-role closure verification: both unchanged npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass with bounded local parallelism, 283/283 tests each, canonical-reader 1/1 and packed acceptance 5/5 each. All 13 executable sources retain 100/100/100/100: 4075/4075 lines and statements, 139/139 functions, 1268/1268 branches. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, packaging, changelog and attestation pass. Corrected targeted tests pass 11/11; pinned pm test --run --progress passes 2/2 linked commands (7/7 SDK-integrity and role tests). Final-source public differential proof passes 22/22 command/export comparisons across immutable 100-item and 89-item corpora; tracker bytes unchanged. classifyStandupItem is the sole lifecycle classifier across work buckets, blocker age/markers and decision reports. Property results: 64 registries, 3840 bucket cases, 61440 section selections, 223200 classifications. Four isolated role reverts fail as documented. Combined adoption removes 105 production-source lines. No missing SDK API or new implementation blocker identified. PR 151 remains ready for updated-head CI and manual review; no merge, release or thread reply."
  "2026-10-26T03:17:05.406Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit on main d1279e294c3bf41694927fd1636e2a02425a9f9a: merged PR #151 (d1279e294c3bf41694927fd1636e2a02425a9f9a, merged 2026-10-25T22:19:19Z). index.ts reads host listAllComplete with full bodies and fresh verified history; status-roles.ts classifyStandupItem centralizes SDK roles/aliases for reports, decisions and blockers. test/sdk-adoption.test.ts and test/status-roles.test.ts cover no-executable reads, expected errors, cache corruption, multiple active/default-open names, terminal decisions and the reviewing regression. All scoped acceptance criteria are represented by the inspected implementation and regressions. Existing behavioural revert evidence is retained; this tracker-only audit changes no runtime functions."
